# The one distribution the apt repository serves, as reprepro reads it.
#
# `Codename: stable` is what a reader types in the source line, and it never moves: a source line
# that has been pasted into someone's /etc/apt/sources.list.d is not something this repository can
# go back and edit. It is not a Debian suite name borrowed for the occasion — it is this
# repository's one channel, and the packages in it are the released versions.
#
# `Limit: -1` keeps every version in the pool rather than only the newest. The pool has to
# accumulate: an apt repository that silently dropped last release's package would break anyone
# pinning a version, and the repository is rebuilt from scratch on every deploy, so the limit is
# the only thing deciding what survives.
#
# `SignWith` is filled in by the site deploy from the APT_SIGNING_KEY_ID repository secret. The
# key id is not written here because this file is public and the id is one of the three things
# the maintainer sets up once; docs/INSTALL.md walks through creating all three.

Origin: Cartogenesis
Label: Cartogenesis
Codename: stable
Suite: stable
Architectures: amd64
Components: main
Description: Cartogenesis desktop builds for Debian and Ubuntu
Limit: -1
SignWith: __APT_SIGNING_KEY_ID__
